# Repository & SQL

Repositories are the **only** place for raw SQL and complex Query Builder logic.

## Layout

```
app/Repositories/Contracts/BlogPostRepositoryInterface.php
app/Repositories/Eloquent/EloquentBlogPostRepository.php
```

Bind interface → implementation in a ServiceProvider. Inject via constructor — never `new`.

## When to use

- Prefer Eloquent on the model for simple CRUD/scopes
- Repository for complex joins, reports, aggregates, shared query logic, or raw SQL Eloquent cannot express cleanly
- Comment briefly why raw SQL was required

## SQL security (required)

- Bind all dynamic values (`?`, `:name`, or Query Builder) — never concatenate
- Whitelist dynamic identifiers (sort columns, tables) — never from raw user input
- Explicit SELECT columns on list/report queries
- Paginate or `limit()` unbounded lists
- Wrap multi-write SQL in `DB::transaction()`

```php
// Good
DB::select('SELECT id, title FROM blog_posts WHERE user_id = ?', [$userId]);

$sort = in_array($sortBy, self::SORTABLE, true) ? $sortBy : 'published_at';
```

## Design

- Typed params and return types on every method
- No HTTP, mail, or cache inside repositories
- Cover new query methods with tests
